{title: All For Me Grog}
{x-alt-title: Well I'm Sick and I'm Tired}
{artist: Irish Traditional}
{copyright: Traditional}
{x-tune: TRADITIONAL}
{x-theme: Sea Shanties}
{x-theme: Drinking Songs}
{x-keyword: Irish}
{x-keyword: Traditional}
{key: D}
{x-recording-url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cs9M1m-dpgM}
{x-recording-title: The Pogues - All For Me Grog}
{x-recording-artist: The Pogues}

{start_of_verse}
Well it's [D]all for me grog, me jolly jolly [A]grog
It's [D]all for me beer and to-[G]bac-[A]co
For I [D]spent all me tin with the [G]lassies drinking [D]gin
Far a-[A]cross the western [D]ocean I must wander
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Where are me boots, me noggin' noggin' boots
They're all gone for beer and tobacco
For the heels they are worn out and the toes are kicked about
And the soles are looking out for better weather
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
It's [D]all for me grog, me jolly jolly [A]grog
It's [D]all for me beer and to-[G]bac-[A]co
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Where is me shirt, me noggin' noggin' shirt
It's all gone for beer and tobacco
For the collar is all worn, and the sleeves they are all torn
And the tail is looking out for better weather
{end_of_verse}
